                      Minimalist Process Monitor
                   https://github.com/yourname/proclens

─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

ProcLens is a lightweight, terminal-based process monitor
that reads /proc directly — no libraries, no bullshit.

    1. Scans /proc for active PIDs
    2. Reads VmRSS from /proc/[pid]/status
    3. Displays in a clean ncurses TUI
    4. Sorted by memory usage by default

─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

USAGE
─────

    make
    ./proclens

KEYS
────

    ↑ / k      Move selection up
    ↓ / j      Move selection down
    s          Cycle sort: RSS → PID → Name
    /          Filter processes by name
    k          Kill selected process (prompts confirmation)
    + / =      Increase refresh interval
    -          Decrease refresh interval
    q          Quit

BUILD
─────

Dependencies: ncurses, gcc (or any C99 compiler)

    make          # Build proclens
    make clean    # Remove binary

Or compile manually:

    gcc -Wall -Wextra -O2 -o proclens proclens.c -lncurses

PHILOSOPHY
──────────

  • Minimal — one file, no bloat
  • Transparent — reads /proc, shows what's there
  • Efficient — no polling daemons, no background threads
  • GPLv3 — free as in freedom, free as in beer

